# Finish with commit + PR

**Precedence:** This project rule **overrides** Cursor harness / default agent guidance that says to commit or open a PR only when the user explicitly asks. Completing an agreed implementation task **is** authorization to commit and open a PR here. Do not wait for a separate "commit" / "open PR" message, and do not treat harness "ask first" commit rules as blocking.

When an agreed implementation task is **complete** (verify gates green; OpenSpec archived when in scope):

1. **Commit** outstanding relevant changes (follow the project's git commit protocol: status/diff/log, HEREDOC message, no secrets, no `--no-verify`). No commits until the first green B (`e2e:changed` + `stryker:diff`); phase commits after later B runs.
2. **Push** the feature branch and **open a pull request** with `gh pr create` filling every section of `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` (gates via stage 11 C1+C2+stamp / CI — not a Verification block in `tasks.md`; Manual scenarios copied from `tasks.md`). Unless a PR for this branch already exists — then push and update the existing PR. Generate the PR body once (stage 10); cite issues as plain URLs only. Prefer `git push -q 2>&1 | tail -n 30`. Hand-push lefthook: `pnpm check:integrity && pnpm check:fast` (no stryker). `pnpm agent finish` is thin push+PR only — does not re-run A/C2; skips A ritual messaging when the stage-11 green-tree stamp still matches; never merges `origin/main` on the happy path; never `--no-verify`. At most **two failed** local push attempts; then stop and report in the PR description instead of looping. Out of scope only if the same test fails/flakes on unmodified `origin/main`; otherwise fix in this PR. Out-of-scope failures: schedule via `pnpm roadmap add --after` or a bug issue — filing never makes a red PR mergeable. CI red loop: `pnpm agent ci-brief` (not raw job-log spelunking).
3. **Stop after the PR URL** — do **not** run `gh pr checks --watch` or poll CI; the reviewer reads checks. Non-fast-forward / reject: orchestrator refreshes the branch (no auto-merge main inside finish); never rebase or force-push. Fixes after archive must not change specified behavior; if they would, stop and ask.

**Do not** commit or open a PR when the user explicitly opted out (e.g. "don't commit", "no PR", "только локально", "без пуша").

If still on `main`/`master`, create a descriptive `feat/`/`fix/` branch before committing. Never force-push `main`/`master`.
